1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:03,000
What if another galaxy hit us?

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,920
It's already on its way.

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:11,480
The Andromeda galaxy is about 2.5 million light-years away. You can see it without a telescope.

4
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:13,640
And it's getting closer.

5
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:17,960
It's coming toward us at about 110 kilometers per second.

6
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,720
The street empties.

7
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:24,760
In about 1 billion years, the brightening Sun will make Earth too hot for life.

8
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:28,280
The trees die. The road turns to dust.

9
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:31,400
Andromeda holds about a trillion stars.

10
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,280
Then a smaller galaxy hits us first.

11
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:40,040
The Large Magellanic Cloud should crash into the Milky Way in about 2.5 billion years.

12
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,680
Now the sky is tearing apart.

13
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:47,400
Even then, stars almost never collide. Space is that empty.

14
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,600
The sky catches fire with newborn stars.

15
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:55,720
Colliding galaxies squeeze their gas clouds, setting off bursts of new stars.

16
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:57,880
The two hearts close in.

17
00:00:57,880 --> 00:01:02,040
Andromeda's central black hole is dozens of times heavier than ours.

18
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:04,760
Together, they become one galaxy.

19
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:08,440
Astronomers already have a name for it: Milkomeda.

20
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:10,040
Or maybe not.

21
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:17,880
In 2025, astronomers ran thousands of simulations. Only about half ended in a crash within 10 billion years.

22
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:19,880
So keep watching the sky.

23
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:22,460
Something else already is.

24
00:01:24,211 --> 00:01:26,231
Wait.

25
00:01:26,731 --> 00:01:29,831
What if a black hole passed through?

26
00:01:30,431 --> 00:01:33,750
What if another galaxy hit us?
